<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18909" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frŭtectum</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frutētum</span></b> , i, n.
		contr. from fruticetum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a place full of shrubs</i> or <i>bushes.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager frutectis aut arboribus obsessus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 11, 3</span></i>
			: rosa silvestris in  frutecto, <i><span class="en">Plin. 25, 2,
				6, § 17</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tenebrosa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. adv. Symm. 2, 872</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acuta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Psych. 443</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Jer. 11, 16</span></i>.—*
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a shrub</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">id frutectum (sc. cinnamum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 30, § 25</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
